# Everything the image must not carry.
#
# The two that matter are .state and .env. .state is live operator config - the
# logos, the team names, the accounts and their password hashes - and baking it
# into an image would put one production's credentials inside every container
# built from it. .env holds the API keys.

.git
.gitattributes
.github

node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Live operator state and secrets. Never in an image.
.state/
.state-backup*/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The Chromium profile holds a Cloudflare clearance bound to the machine that
# earned it. Copying one into an image guarantees it is wrong everywhere.
.playwright-profile/

# Local notes and scratch output.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
deployment.md
tools/probe-output/
*.log
*.hidden

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
deployment.md
README.md
